  "question": {
    "text": "Let $\\mathrm{T}_{\\mathrm{r}}$ be the $\\mathrm{r}^{\\text {th }}$ term of an A.P. If for some $\\mathrm{m}, \\mathrm{T}_{\\mathrm{m}}=\\frac{1}{25}, \\mathrm{~T}_{25}=\\frac{1}{20}$, and $20 \\sum_{\\mathrm{r}=1}^{25} \\mathrm{~T}_{\\mathrm{r}}=13$, then $5 \\mathrm{~m} \\sum_{\\mathrm{r}=\\mathrm{m}}^{2 \\mathrm{~m}} \\mathrm{~T}_{\\mathrm{r}}$ is equal to"
